/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Workflows_SharedInfrastructure Shared Build Infrastructure
 * @ingroup DspCore_Workflows
 * @brief DspCore's pinned RoModularBuild integration and ownership boundary.
 *
 * DspCore consumes `tools/RoModularBuild` as a Git submodule pinned to a tagged
 * revision. Initialize it after cloning:
 *
 * @code{.bash}
 * git submodule update --init --recursive
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCoreSharedInfrastructureOwnership Ownership
 *
 * RoModularBuild owns project-independent mechanics:
 *
 * - native compiler and generator preset bases;
 * - generic GNU Arm Embedded and AVR-GCC toolchains;
 * - configure, build, test, install, and clean workflow engines; and
 * - reusable CI composite actions.
 *
 * DspCore owns project policy:
 *
 * - public preset names and `DSPCORE_*` feature options;
 * - Foundation discovery and version compatibility;
 * - the `DspCore::DspCore` package, export, and downstream consumer validation;
 * - source modules, tests, examples, Doxygen, and release policy; and
 * - exact firmware, board, and hardware validation fixtures.
 *
 * @section DspCoreSharedInfrastructureAdapters Adapters
 *
 * Public commands under `scripts/` remain stable. Thin adapters provide DspCore's
 * roots and option names to the shared engines. Local toolchain wrappers map
 * the established `DSPCORE_*` cache variables to the project-independent
 * `ROMODULAR_*` variables before including the shared implementation.
 *
 * This compatibility layer prevents the infrastructure migration from
 * changing DspCore's public presets, build directories, or cache interface.
 * Debug and Release remain configurations of one platform preset.
 *
 * @section DspCoreSharedInfrastructurePin Updating the Pin
 *
 * Treat `tools/RoModularBuild` as read-only from DspCore. Update its gitlink only
 * as an explicit dependency change, pin a tagged revision, and rerun native,
 * package-consumer, embedded compile/link, and documentation validation.
 */
